---
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Row from "../components/Row.astro";

const blogs = await getCollection('blog');
---

<Base>
  <header class="masthead">
    <h2>What is this?</h2>
    <p class="meta">
    These are my personal notes about the stuff I code. After I build something fairly monumental, or something interesting, I'll write about my experience here. 
    It'll be messy and random, but hopefully it helps me internalize what I build.
    </p>
    <br>
    <p class="meta">
    Keep in mind that this will be 
    informal, and some parts plain wrong (hopefully not!) so don't use this as a tutorial or source of truth please! 
    If there is an egregious error of some sort, feel free to email me about it.
    Lastly, my LaTeX might not be the best, but hopefully that improves in the future.
    </p>
  </header>
  <div class="rows">
    {
      blogs.map((blog) => (
        <Row
          href={`/blogs/${blog.id}`}
          title={blog.data.title}
          blurb={blog.data.blurb}
          meta={String(blog.data.date.getFullYear())}
        />
      ))
    }
  </div>
</Base>
